# Dart & Flutter Conventions

## Style
- `lowerCamelCase` members; `UpperCamelCase` types; `snake_case` files.
- Prefer `const` constructors; immutable domain entities.
- Explicit types on public APIs; avoid dynamic except at true boundaries.
- No `print` in production paths; use a logging abstraction (adapter).

## SOLID / DRY
- One public type’s primary job per file when practical.
- Share logic via use cases / domain services — not copy-paste across TV/Companion.
- Prefer composition over deep widget inheritance.

## Widgets
- Keep widgets **small and dumb**; lift state / orchestration out.
- Put reusable UI in `lib/core/widgets` (FocusableCard, StateScaffold, etc.).
- Avoid mega-screens: extract sections and overlays.

## State & navigation
- Do not introduce Riverpod/Bloc/Provider/go_router/etc. until approved.
- Until then, keep composition root in `lib/app` and feature presentation local.

## Tests
- Unit-test domain/use cases; widget-test shared widgets and critical screens.
- Mirror feature paths under `test/`.
